<h1 id="gamma-friends-a-guide">Gamma &amp; Friends: A &quot;Guide&quot;</h1>
<p>Gamma is a <em>small</em> language with <strong>big</strong> ideas, and
text may wrap over several lines. Use *stars* literally,
or write snake_case_names without surprise; <strong>bold</strong> and <em>emphasis</em> work too.</p>
<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
<ul>
<li>Algebraic <strong>effects</strong> with <code>handlers</code></li>
<li>Tagged unions &amp; <code>match</code></li>
<li>No hidden &lt;allocation&gt;</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li>Install it</li>
<li>Write <code>main :: fn()</code></li>
<li>Read the <a href="https://example.com/a?b=1&amp;c=2">guide</a></li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p>Quote: &quot;keep it <em>simple</em>&quot;</p>
<p>and short</p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
<h3 id="unicode-caf-na-ve-ok">Unicode: café ☕ naïve — ok?</h3>
<pre><code>if a &lt; b &amp;&amp; c &gt; d {
    print(&quot;&lt;b&gt;&quot;)
}
</code></pre>
<p>Final paragraph with an unclosed *star and a lone [bracket.</p>
